<title>EGYPT: EGYPT MONEY SUPPLY UP 14.6 PCT IN YR TO END MAY.</title>
<headline>EGYPT MONEY SUPPLY UP 14.6 PCT IN YR TO END MAY.</headline>
<dateline>CAIRO 1997-08-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Egyptian broad money supply grew 14.6 percent in the year ending May 1997, from 13.7 percent in the year to April 1997, the Central Bank of Egypt said in a bulletin available on Monday.</p>
<p>Total money supply, including quasi-money and foreign currency deposits, was 191.373 billion pounds ($56.4 billion) at end-May against 187.380 billion at end-April.</p>
<p>Following figures, in billions of pounds, were supplied by the central bank.</p>
<p>					 May 97    April 97   May 96</p>
<p>    Total money supply	   191.373   187.380    166.937</p>
<p>    Money			     38.873    38.593     35.116</p>
<p>    Quasi-money		    152.500   148.787    131.821</p>
<p>    Year-on-year growth (pct)   +14.6     +13.7	 --</p>
<p>    Month-on-month growth (pct) +2.13     +1.86	0.90</p>
<p>-- Cairo newsroom +20 2 578 3290/1 ($ = 3.392 Egyptian Pounds)</p>
</text>
